# Line endings — see CLAUDE.md 6.4.
#
# Every text file is stored LF in the repository and checked out LF. Declaring
# it here makes it a property of the repo rather than of whoever cloned it:
# core.autocrlf is a per-installation setting (Git for Windows ships it as
# `true`, plain Git as `false`), so without this file the working tree's line
# endings depend on the machine. On a clone with core.autocrlf=false the result
# is a CRLF working tree against LF blobs, and `git status` reports every text
# file as modified — the same diff regenerated on every platform switch.
#
# eol=lf rather than eol=native: the toolchain is LF-native end to end. CI runs
# on Linux runners, scripts/cf-build.sh runs in Cloudflare's Linux build image,
# and rustfmt / svelte-check / Vite all emit LF. A CRLF working tree buys
# nothing here and costs a diff whenever the platform changes.

*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never end-of-line converted, never diffed as text.
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.webp          binary
*.bmp           binary
*.gif           binary
*.tif           binary
*.tiff          binary
*.ico           binary
*.wasm          binary
*.zip           binary
*.zst           binary
*.fln           binary

# Shell scripts run in a Linux build image; a CRLF shebang breaks them, so LF
# is not a preference here but a correctness requirement.
*.sh            text eol=lf
